---
// Generated by GSA-Per-Diem/tools/export_legal_to_website.mjs from the app's legal.json. Edit that file instead.
type Props = {
  contactEmail: string;
};

const { contactEmail } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="legal-content">
  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Use apply to US Per Diem (the "App") from Restart Apps ("we", "us", or "our").
      By using the App, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>2. Use of the App</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the App for personal, internal business, or travel-planning purposes. You may not
      misuse the App, interfere with its operation, attempt to reverse engineer it except where
      permitted by law, or use it in a way that violates applicable laws or third-party rights.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>3. Rate data and reports</h2>
    <p>
      The App displays per diem rates published by the <a
      href="https://www.gsa.gov/travel/plan-a-trip/per-diem-rates">U.S. General Services
      Administration (GSA)</a> and the <a
      href="https://www.travel.dod.mil/Travel-Transportation-Rates/Per-Diem/Per-Diem-Rate-Lookup/">Defense
      Travel Management Office (DTMO)</a>. The App is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored
      by GSA, DTMO, the Department of Defense, or any other government agency.
    </p>
    <p>
      Rates, calculations, PDF exports, and CSV exports are provided for informational convenience
      only. We do not guarantee that rates are current, complete, or suitable for reimbursement,
      tax, payroll, accounting, legal, or official travel purposes. You are responsible for
      verifying rates and reimbursement rules with the official source or your organization before
      relying on them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Trip reports apply general rules: 75% of the meals and incidental expenses (M&amp;IE) rate on
      the first and last travel day and no lodging on the final day, using the rate in effect for
      each date. They do not account for agency-specific policies, meals provided to you, lodging
      taxes, actual expense or conference lodging allowances, or other special rules.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>4. Advertisements and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      The App may display advertisements through Google AdMob and uses other third-party services
      for consent, diagnostics, analytics, app distribution, or rate retrieval. We are not
      responsible for third-party content, services, policies, outages, or data practices. How the
      App handles information is described in the Privacy Policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>5. Exports and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      The App can generate report files on your device. You are responsible for reviewing exported
      files before sharing them and for choosing where those files are stored or sent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>6. App stores</h2>
    <p>
      Your use of the App is also subject to the terms of the store you downloaded it from. If you
      downloaded the App from the Apple App Store, Apple's <a
      href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Standard Licensed
      Application End User License Agreement</a> also applies, and Apple has no obligation to
      provide maintenance or support for the App. Apple, Google, and Samsung are not parties to
      these Terms and are not responsible for the App or its content.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>7. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The App is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, express or
      implied. We do not warrant that the App will be uninterrupted, error-free, or always
      available.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental,
      consequential, special, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for loss of data, profits,
      business, reimbursement, or travel expenses arising from your use of or inability to use the
      App.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>9. Changes to these Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use of the App after updated Terms are
      posted means you accept the updated Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the United States, without regard to conflict-of-law
      principles, unless applicable law requires otherwise.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>11. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms can be sent to <a
      href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
